WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.300
Coconut rolls, banana bread and rock buns from a small oven.

2
00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:09.300
This is the video for module 3 of Basic Baking and Snacks Production.

3
00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:25.720
Coconut bread uses cheap local coconut and sells well by the piece. Blend grated coconut with warm water and squeeze out about 300 ml of milk. Fresh coconut milk spoils quickly, so use it within a few hours.

4
00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:37.820
Mix the dough and knead it for 10 to 12 minutes. Stretch a small piece: if it goes thin enough to let light through without tearing, it is ready. That is the windowpane test.

5
00:00:39.070 --> 00:00:42.890
Cover it and let it prove until doubled, usually about 1 hour.

6
00:00:44.140 --> 00:00:51.590
Weigh the whole dough and divide it into 12 pieces of about 80 g, so every roll is the same size and price.

7
00:00:52.840 --> 00:01:03.500
Prove again until puffy, brush with milk or egg, and bake at about 180 to 190 degrees on your oven thermometer, for 15 to 20 minutes.

8
00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:14.180
A baked roll is golden, and the base sounds hollow when tapped. Cool it on a rack for at least an hour. Bagging warm bread traps steam and invites mould.

9
00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:24.880
To make more, do not guess. For example, Efe in Warri has an order for 30 rolls of 80 g. That is 2,400 g of dough.

10
00:01:26.130 --> 00:01:39.720
The recipe makes 995 g. 2,400 divided by 995 is 2.41, and she rounds up a little to 2.5, to cover dough that sticks to the bowl.

11
00:01:40.970 --> 00:01:52.840
She multiplies every ingredient by 2.5. Flour becomes 1,250 g. Weigh scaled yeast and salt carefully, because too much salt slows the yeast.

12
00:01:54.090 --> 00:02:03.240
She gets 31 rolls, one spare to cut and check. Her bowl is too small, so she mixes two smaller doughs and bakes them 20 minutes apart.

13
00:02:04.490 --> 00:02:16.240
Black-speckled bananas are cheap and perfect: the riper, the sweeter. Reject any with mould or a fermented smell. Weigh the peeled banana, because counting gives uneven loaves.

14
00:02:17.490 --> 00:02:23.720
In one bowl, whisk the flour, baking soda and salt. Weigh the soda, because too much tastes soapy.

15
00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:29.300
In the other, mix the mashed banana, melted margarine, sugar and eggs.

16
00:02:30.550 --> 00:02:39.850
Pour the wet into the dry and fold only until no dry flour shows. Small lumps are fine. Over-mixing gives a tough loaf full of tunnels.

17
00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:51.680
Bake at about 175 degrees for 50 to 60 minutes, until a skewer comes out clean. If the top browns too fast, cover it loosely with foil.

18
00:02:52.930 --> 00:02:56.430
A whole loaf needs less wrapping and keeps longer uncut.

19
00:02:57.680 --> 00:03:14.130
Slices often earn more per loaf. For example, Yetunde in Abeokuta supplies a cafe with 30 slices every Friday: three loaves of 10 slices. Cool completely, slice evenly and wrap each one. If you add nuts, say so on the label.

20
00:03:15.380 --> 00:03:26.790
For rock buns, rub cold margarine into the flour and make a stiff dough. Put rough heaps on the tray and do not smooth them. Warm margarine or a wet dough makes them spread flat.

21
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:44.940
For coconut candy, dissolve sugar in water, then stop stirring and let it boil. At light amber, add the coconut, stir, and scoop small pieces with two spoons. For example, Grace in Calabar makes both from one coconut: 42 items for her stall.

22
00:03:46.190 --> 00:03:55.240
Cooking sugar gets far hotter than boiling water, and it sticks to skin. Wear long sleeves, use a long-handled spoon, and keep children out.

23
00:03:56.490 --> 00:04:00.070
Never taste from the pot, and never use your fingers to shape it.

24
00:04:01.320 --> 00:04:15.020
If hot sugar touches skin, cool it under cool running water for 20 minutes. Do not peel off stuck sugar, and do not put butter, oil, toothpaste or raw egg on a burn. Get medical help for large burns.

25
00:04:16.270 --> 00:04:32.520
To remember. Knead to the windowpane test and divide by weight. Scale by total dough weight. Fold banana batter gently. Cool everything before bagging. And treat hot sugar with great care. Fresh coconut shortens shelf life, so sell quickly.

26
00:04:33.770 --> 00:04:47.430
Now practise. Bake a batch of coconut rolls and work out the quantities for 45. Bake and slice a banana loaf and keep a 4-day log. Then make rock buns and coconut candy from one coconut.

27
00:04:47.780 --> 00:04:49.720
Continue with the lessons below.
